{
  "note": "Cross-client vectors for the x.approval wire pair. Each body is the EXACT wire string; the shared, app and CLI suites all parse these same bytes — agreement on a fixture, not on prose. Schema: packages/shared/src/approval-envelope.ts. On the authvectors.json pattern.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "request",
      "kind": "x.approval",
      "valid": true,
      "note": "A realistic command ask: the payload is commandPayload’s `${command}\\ncwd: ${cwd}` verbatim, the verbs are the approve/deny pair, the TTL is the CLI default (600s) inside the clamp.",
      "body": "{\"tcm\":\"x.approval\",\"q\":\"01J8MEAPPR0VAQ4X2C6TKN9RFV\",\"k\":\"exec\",\"p\":\"npm test -- --watch=false\\ncwd: /Users/op/tacendum\",\"x\":600,\"s\":\"s-7c2e\",\"a\":[\"approve\",\"deny\"]}"
    },
    {
      "name": "answer",
      "kind": "x.approval.answer",
      "valid": true,
      "note": "The structured answer, echoing q and the tag. n is the byte length of the request payload as rendered — a bug detector, not a security control.",
      "body": "{\"tcm\":\"x.approval.answer\",\"q\":\"01J8MEAPPR0VAQ4X2C6TKN9RFV\",\"v\":\"approve\",\"s\":\"s-7c2e\",\"n\":49}"
    },
    {
      "name": "request-overcap",
      "kind": "x.approval",
      "valid": false,
      "note": "Payload one over MAX_APPROVAL_PAYLOAD_BYTES: the schema refuses it, and every shipped client still shows NOTHING for it (x. prefix drop) — the CLI never composes one (over-cap is an instant deny).",
      "body": "{\"tcm\":\"x.approval\",\"q\":\"01J8MEAPPR0VAQ4X2C6TKN9RFV\",\"k\":\"exec\",\"p\":\"\",\"x\":600,\"s\":\"s-7c2e\",\"a\":[\"approve\",\"deny\"]}"
    },
    {
      "name": "request-wrong-tag",
      "kind": "x.approval",
      "valid": false,
      "note": "s must be the sessionTag shape (s- plus four hex), never a raw host session id — the guard sessionTag exists to enforce.",
      "body": "{\"tcm\":\"x.approval\",\"q\":\"01J8MEAPPR0VAQ4X2C6TKN9RFV\",\"k\":\"exec\",\"p\":\"npm test -- --watch=false\\ncwd: /Users/op/tacendum\",\"x\":600,\"s\":\"aaaaaaaa-1111-4111-8111-111111111111\",\"a\":[\"approve\",\"deny\"]}"
    },
    {
      "name": "request-unknown-verb",
      "kind": "x.approval",
      "valid": true,
      "note": "A future verb in the a array is ACCEPTED by the schema (a verb is a bounded string, not an enum — a verb costs the answer, never the frame). The consumer-side rule the suites document: a verb a build does not recognise renders no button and NEVER reads as approve.",
      "body": "{\"tcm\":\"x.approval\",\"q\":\"01J8MEAPPR0VAQ4X2C6TKN9RFV\",\"k\":\"exec\",\"p\":\"npm test -- --watch=false\\ncwd: /Users/op/tacendum\",\"x\":600,\"s\":\"s-7c2e\",\"a\":[\"approve\",\"deny\",\"escalate\"]}"
    },
    {
      "name": "answer-unknown-verb",
      "kind": "x.approval.answer",
      "valid": true,
      "note": "Same rule from the answer side: v parses (bounded string), and the CLI applies it only if it is a verb it knows — unknown NEVER reads as approve (attend.ts ApprovalDecision fails closed).",
      "body": "{\"tcm\":\"x.approval.answer\",\"q\":\"01J8MEAPPR0VAQ4X2C6TKN9RFV\",\"v\":\"escalate\",\"s\":\"s-7c2e\",\"n\":49}"
    }
  ]
}
